{
  "uid": "cloudpipe-karpenter",
  "title": "CloudPipe — Karpenter Autoscaler",
  "description": "How the cluster grows and shrinks: nodes Karpenter provisions, spot interruptions it absorbs, nodepool capacity headroom, and the nodes it voluntarily removes to save money.",
  "tags": [
    "cloudpipe",
    "karpenter",
    "infrastructure"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 900,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### 📈 How the cluster grows and shrinks\n\nNodes are not kept running for the pipeline. **Karpenter** creates machines when pods need them and deletes them when they go idle, mostly on **spot** capacity, which AWS can reclaim at short notice.\n\nSo three things matter:\n\n- **Provisioning speed** — how fast a pending pod gets a machine\n- **Interruptions** — how often spot capacity is reclaimed, and whether pods survived it\n- **Headroom** — how close each nodepool is to its ceiling\n\n**Blank panels usually mean an idle cluster**, not a fault: between batches there are no Karpenter nodes at all, so anything grouped by nodepool has nothing to show."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Karpenter nodes now",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "count(kube_node_labels{label_karpenter_sh_nodepool!=\"\"})",
          "legendFormat": "Nodes"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Nodes Karpenter currently manages. ZERO is the normal resting state — between batches the cluster runs only its static managed nodegroups, which Karpenter does not own and which carry no nodepool label."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Pods waiting for capacity",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum(kube_pod_status_phase{namespace=\"argo-workflows\", phase=\"Pending\"})",
          "legendFormat": "Pending"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Pipeline pods that cannot be scheduled right now — Pending in the argo-workflows namespace. Scoped to the pipeline deliberately: Karpenter does provision for any unschedulable pod cluster-wide, but system pods pending for their own reasons only add noise to the question this dashboard exists to answer. Matches the equivalent panel on Infrastructure Health, so the two agree."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Spot reclaims (1 h)",
      "description": "Spot instances AWS took back in the last hour. Expected and survivable — the pipeline retries interrupted work — but a sustained spike is worth correlating against failures.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "ceil(sum(increase(karpenter_nodeclaims_disrupted_total{reason=\"spot_interrupted\"}[1h])))",
          "legendFormat": "Interruptions"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Nodes drained (1 h)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "ceil(sum(increase(karpenter_nodes_drained_total[1h])))",
          "legendFormat": "Drained"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 3
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Nodes Karpenter cordoned and emptied in the last hour, for any reason — spot reclaim, consolidation, or expiry. Draining is orderly: pods are evicted and rescheduled. Compare with the removal panel below to see which cause dominated."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "⚡ Spot interruptions",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Interruption notices, by type",
      "description": "SQS message volume, not distinct nodes — AWS redelivers each notice several times. Use this for queue health; use the 'Spot Interruptions' stat for the true node count. 'no_op' dominates by volume and is dimmed.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (message_type) (rate(karpenter_interruption_received_messages_total[5m])) * 3600",
          "legendFormat": "{{message_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "spot_interrupted"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "orange",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "rebalance_recommendation"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "yellow",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "no_op"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "text",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "How long interruption notices sat in the queue",
      "description": "How long an interruption message sits in SQS before Karpenter processes it. The spot interruption notice gives ~2 minutes of warning, so this is the slice of that budget lost to queueing — elevated values here shorten the window pods have to drain gracefully.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-prometheus",
        "type": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(karpenter_interruption_message_queue_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(karpenter_interruption_message_queue_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(karpenter_interruption_message_queue_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        }
      }
    },
